WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.670
(Chūka Ichiban)

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.940
For the legendary cookware,

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:36.140
the four-round banquet cooking battle

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:36.950
against Dark Cooking Society.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:39.760
In first round it was about soup.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.440
Sanjie took the first win.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.450
The second round is about dim sum.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:46.620
Chef Xie goes for the battle.

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:48.160
However,

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:49.940
he got an unexpected opponent,

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.910
the legendary Pastry King Luogen.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:55.620
Besides...

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.990
(Steamed buns)

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:02.830
Not good.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.290
The least expected category

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:06.850
was hit.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:10.310
Pastry King Luogen

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:12.980
1,600 Year-Old Spirit-Calming Chinese Steamed Bun

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:25.510
Looks like it’s not your lucky day.

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:26.500
Young man.

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.890
What do you mean not good, Lei En?

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:35.080
The Bailuo family was the progenitor of dim sum.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:36.640
Their first generation

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:38.040
worked for Zhuge Kongming

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:41.020
as his chef

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:42.420
in the Three Kingdoms period.

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:45.670
When Kongming

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:48.250
led his army back from the south,

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:50.130
to pacify the raging river

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.560
in their way,

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:54.640
they made tributes with flour

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:55.790
for the God of River.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:58.120
That’s the origin of steamed buns.

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:03.330
So, the first steamed bun chef was...

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:05.550
His ancestor.

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:10.330
In other words,

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:11.520
steamed buns are

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:14.010
what he is best at.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:18.390
How will Chef Xie deal with

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:21.310
such a powerful opponent?

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:22.810
Young man.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.350
You'd better give up now.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.550
Interesting.

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:30.070
Let’s battle it out.

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:35.650
Since the battle with Mao,

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:37.490
I haven’t had such an interesting battle.

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:39.640
You, fossil geezer.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:41.540
I’ll add you

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:43.100
to those I have defeated.

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:44.160
Chef Xie.

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:46.420
Yes, keep it up!

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:48.360
Stop bragging, you brat.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:49.850
Listen.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:52.560
You stand no chance to win.

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:56.320
Save your rubbish talk.

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:07.380
The second round, dim sum battle,

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:08.340
now begins.

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:19.490
It begins.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.780
A steamed bun battle across centuries.

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:50.390
Both hands?

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:51.960
Chef Xie’s arms are strong enough

00:04:52.010 --> 00:04:54.840
to wield his heavy steel stick.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:56.280
So, he’s powerful

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.460
when kneading the dough.

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:03.940
I didn’t think

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:04.560
you’d knead two doughs

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:07.000
simultaneously with both hands.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:10.310
You live up to your repute as the Number One.

00:05:13.170 --> 00:05:14.810
Why haven’t you started?

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:16.030
Geezer.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.110
I’m very honored to battle

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:20.420
against the legendary Pastry King.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:22.550
I wish we could have met earlier.

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:25.210
You are too old now.

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:27.240
I doubt if you can knead a dough well.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:28.200
You...

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:32.530
Who do you think I am?

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:34.780
If you are number one in the Continent,

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:36.980
then I’m number one in the world.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:42.300
The Steal Bar Xie.

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:44.610
Since you want to learn secret techniques,

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:47.250
I may show you some.

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:04.650
Dough is not kneaded by strength.

00:06:05.890 --> 00:06:07.570
The rotation of fingers,

00:06:09.240 --> 00:06:11.110
the arm,

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.580
and the stick.

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:20.350
That’s to say,

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:23.090
the essence of dim sum

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:24.910
lies in rotation.

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:27.030
How huge and deep

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:28.730
the rotation you make

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.170
shows the capability of a dim sum chef.

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:36.660
The dough!

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:48.210
What?

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:50.390
The Bailuo family’s secret.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:57.460
Bailuo Snake Rotation Technique.

00:06:57.460 --> 00:06:58.790
(Bailuo Snake Rotation Technique)

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:00.330
Bailuo Snake Rotation Technique.

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:01.890
I see.

00:07:02.170 --> 00:07:02.830
He uses

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.190
the force of rotation

00:07:04.280 --> 00:07:05.660
and repeats it

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:06.810
to make the dough extend.

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:08.850
He wants to knead it

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:09.920
as smooth and soft as possible.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:16.640
That’s the legendary Pastry King Luogen.

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:18.570
It... It’s amazing.

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:24.010
What's wrong, boy?

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:26.140
Why do you stop?

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:28.990
It’d be boring

00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:30.670
if you didn’t do this,

00:07:30.980 --> 00:07:32.310
fossil geezer.

00:07:36.670 --> 00:07:39.300
Great! Chef Xie is great too!

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:41.020
By the way, Mao.

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:43.670
Steamed buns, dumplings and shumai,

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.070
what’s the difference of them?

00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:46.450
The biggest difference

00:07:46.970 --> 00:07:48.390
is the thick and fluffy skin.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:50.400
As I told you,

00:07:50.630 --> 00:07:54.170
shumai’s skin is like the silk rope

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:55.880
gently keeping the flavor of stuffing inside.

00:07:56.830 --> 00:07:57.800
Dumpling’s skin must

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:00.380
keep the stuffing’s taste inside tightly,

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:02.490
like a leather bag.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:04.030
In comparison,

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:07.510
bun’s skin is like a feather quilt.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:10.000
Quilt?

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:12.660
The well leavened soft skin

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:14.350
of buns

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:16.450
determines half of the taste.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.540
To leaven the skin,

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:20.360
yeast is used.

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:21.380
Yeast?

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:24.890
This is made from fermented potatoes.

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:27.520
Add yeast into dough

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:28.520
and leave it for some time.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.310
The dough will be leavened.

00:08:45.980 --> 00:08:47.160
I know the skin is very important.

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:47.970
What about the stuffing?

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:48.750
The stuffing inside

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:51.090
is crucial to the taste as well.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:54.530
The juice must be enough

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:56.520
to seep in the skin.

00:08:57.340 --> 00:08:59.570
Guangdong Super Chef,

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:00.480
Liu Maoxing.

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:01.600
Yes.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:07.570
You do know a lot.

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:10.890
But yeast isn’t the only thing

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.320
to leaven dough.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:20.600
Do you know this,

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:22.300
Liu Maoxing?

00:09:23.710 --> 00:09:24.730
That is...

00:09:25.530 --> 00:09:28.080
This is the soul of steamed buns.

00:09:28.600 --> 00:09:29.670
Old Dough?

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:31.280
Exactly.

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:34.240
You know the value

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:35.540
of Old Dough, too.

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.710
Mao, what is Old Dough?

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:38.820
What is it, Mao?

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:42.210
I heard that, many dim sum chefs

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:43.200
remain some Old Dough

00:09:43.240 --> 00:09:45.070
when they make steamed buns.

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:47.800
Yes, then knead it in

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.240
when they make buns next time.

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:51.070
That is, using the previous yeast

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:53.050
to leaven a new dough.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:56.310
Is that so-called Old Dough?

00:09:56.710 --> 00:09:59.700
They say the older the dough is, the better it is.

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:01.880
Because the older the yeast is,

00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:03.670
the more delicate the skin is.

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:05.350
And it's tastier.

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:07.730
You mean Luogen’s Old Dough is...

00:10:07.930 --> 00:10:09.180
Yes, you are right.

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:12.290
That Old Dough was from his ancestors,

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:14.680
the Three Kingdoms period

00:10:14.730 --> 00:10:16.030
1,600 years ago.

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:18.100
1,600 years!

00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:22.210
You have keen eyes, Liu Maoxing.

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:24.310
This is the top yeast

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:25.260
of my Bailuo family

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:28.550
passed down

00:10:28.630 --> 00:10:30.140
from 1,600 years ago.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:31.960
Shuhan Old Dough.

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:33.600
Shuhan Old Dough?

00:10:34.090 --> 00:10:37.260
(Shu)

00:10:37.260 --> 00:10:50.730
(Shu Wei Wu)

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:52.810
There is

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:55.360
no older yeast than this in the world.

00:10:55.990 --> 00:10:57.810
Only buns made with this can be

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:01.370
called number one in the Continent.

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:08.410
Look carefully.

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:11.640
The dough added with Shuhan Old Dough!

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:23.910
It seems alive.

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:50.950
(Chūka Ichiban)

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:59.150
Its expansion is amazing.

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.840
This is the power

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:02.800
of 1600-year-old yeast.

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:05.430
It’s a evenly kneaded

00:12:06.090 --> 00:12:07.850
and perfectly leavened dough.

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:08.940
That way, he can make

00:12:08.990 --> 00:12:10.110
the perfect buns

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:12.000
that no one ever tastes.

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:14.530
This battle is secured.

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:21.440
Chef Xie.

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:24.130
What's so funny, young man?

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:27.740
You treasure

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:29.320
some 1600-year-old

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:30.410
moldy yeast

00:12:30.460 --> 00:12:32.280
and see it as a trump card.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:34.140
You are a fossil

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:35.000
who would do that.

00:12:35.200 --> 00:12:36.110
What did you say?

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:38.410
You’re bluffing.

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:40.370
Bluffing or not,

00:12:40.430 --> 00:12:42.770
you’ll see when the result is out.

00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:43.800
Chef Xie.

00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:45.440
I can do this.

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.020
Don’t worry, Mao.

00:12:46.520 --> 00:12:48.200
My bun skin is ready, too.

00:12:48.710 --> 00:12:49.800
Really?

00:12:50.190 --> 00:12:50.890
What kind of skin?

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:52.320
This.

00:12:58.660 --> 00:12:59.880
Why is it so flat?

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:01.790
Is it your bun skin?

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:04.610
It’s not shumai’s skin you are making!

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:06.160
How can you defeat him

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:08.080
with such flat skin?

00:13:08.130 --> 00:13:09.210
Chef Xie!

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:10.100
Chef Xie.

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:14.180
I don't know what you are planning.

00:13:14.700 --> 00:13:16.330
But you can’t win

00:13:16.380 --> 00:13:17.980
just by being creative.

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:20.680
You can’t win

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:22.330
with a wrong way of cooking.

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:23.250
Right or wrong,

00:13:23.300 --> 00:13:26.180
it’s good as long as people like it.

00:13:26.460 --> 00:13:27.010
Geezer.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:29.100
Battle with Mao someday

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:32.020
and you’ll know it.

00:13:32.340 --> 00:13:33.080
Chef Xie.

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:34.870
Watch it, Mao.

00:13:35.550 --> 00:13:36.610
I’ll make

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:38.190
mysterious buns

00:13:38.240 --> 00:13:39.030
that surprise you.

00:13:46.210 --> 00:13:48.800
Okay. They’ve prepared skins.

00:13:49.190 --> 00:13:50.110
Next is stuffing.

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:53.080
Generally, ground pork is used

00:13:53.170 --> 00:13:54.530
combined with other ingredients.

00:13:54.950 --> 00:13:56.890
I wonder what Chef Xie will use.

00:13:58.160 --> 00:13:59.620
We’re going to see

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:01.170
Chef Xie’s amazing bun-making skills.

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:08.250
Bamboo.

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:10.000
I see.

00:14:11.520 --> 00:14:12.870
Here we go.

00:14:13.210 --> 00:14:14.560
Isn’t that beef?

00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:17.140
He doesn’t use pork, Mao.

00:14:17.240 --> 00:14:18.610
Is it okay?

00:14:18.950 --> 00:14:19.540
No, Silang.

00:14:19.680 --> 00:14:20.970
Using beef is right.

00:14:21.620 --> 00:14:23.080
Beef is the best to

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:25.160
make the stuffing juicy.

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:27.120
I would have done the same.

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:28.150
So,

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:30.910
Chef Xie is going to show his staff skill!

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:31.990
Come on.

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:32.730
Show us

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:34.500
how you use the awesome steel staff.

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:38.960
Hurry. Stand behind.

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:40.190
Or you’ll be blown down.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:50.320
What is he doing?

00:14:51.220 --> 00:14:52.760
That staff is very heavy.

00:14:52.860 --> 00:14:54.300
Just look carefully.

00:14:54.570 --> 00:14:56.000
He is going to

00:14:56.050 --> 00:14:58.580
beat the beef into pulp with it.

00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:01.250
That is his best technique.

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:09.640
Why does he stop?

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:20.630
Chef Xie.

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:22.210
Why don’t you use the steel staff?

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:23.410
No.

00:15:24.710 --> 00:15:26.210
I was just warming up.

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:29.390
Since we are gathered here,

00:15:29.990 --> 00:15:31.070
I’d like to show everyone

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:32.200
how I use my staff.

00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:33.270
It is

00:15:33.390 --> 00:15:34.860
a special offer for you.

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:37.350
Are you going to mince beef

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:38.920
with the knife?

00:15:39.530 --> 00:15:40.610
I’m not mincing beef.

00:15:57.230 --> 00:15:58.040
Steak.

00:15:58.260 --> 00:15:59.800
Steak for buns?

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:03.350
I’m confused.

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:06.230
Young man.

00:16:06.340 --> 00:16:09.300
Will you use the flat skin

00:16:09.350 --> 00:16:10.360
to wrap meat?

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:11.660
Let me make it clear.

00:16:11.810 --> 00:16:12.720
Making those fake buns

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:14.590
is off the topic.

00:16:24.360 --> 00:16:25.640
You know you can’t win,

00:16:25.690 --> 00:16:27.370
so you have given up.

00:16:27.850 --> 00:16:30.520
I’m making such interesting things.

00:16:30.650 --> 00:16:31.240
What?

00:16:32.260 --> 00:16:33.280
You can’t even tell

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:34.150
what I am making.

00:16:35.010 --> 00:16:35.760
You, the Pastry King,

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:36.620
are not qualified.

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:41.380
They say

00:16:41.430 --> 00:16:43.350
many dim sum chefs are arrogant.

00:16:43.650 --> 00:16:46.340
Nothing has changed from the past.

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:47.870
Alright.

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:50.650
My buns are almost done.

00:16:54.130 --> 00:16:55.360
Eight casseroles?

00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:56.540
Why?

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:59.290
Why are casseroles used for buns?

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:00.220
It's weird.

00:17:01.250 --> 00:17:01.930
I got it.

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:04.310
What's the reason, Lei En?

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:06.350
Look carefully, Mao.

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:12.600
Let me show you

00:17:13.030 --> 00:17:16.000
the ultimate dim sum of the Bailuo family.

00:17:19.700 --> 00:17:22.710
What are the bamboos for?

00:17:54.400 --> 00:17:57.050
Bailuo is serious. Here it comes.

00:17:57.620 --> 00:17:58.570
I’ve been in Dark Cooking Society,

00:17:58.820 --> 00:18:00.910
but I’ve never seen it.

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:02.630
The legendary...

00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:10.670
Secret Buns.

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:12.200
Secret Buns?

00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:14.400
What do you mean?

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:16.680
It was passed down

00:18:16.730 --> 00:18:18.510
from 1600 years ago in his family,

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:19.730
the secret of secrets,

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:22.850
the legendary buns.

00:18:23.430 --> 00:18:24.390
Great.

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:26.560
I have a chance to see such great buns!

00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:27.220
Hey.

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:30.150
Why are you so excited?

00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:32.250
Because it’s awesome.

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:33.620
I’m really excited.

00:18:34.770 --> 00:18:36.950
The number one Super Dim Sum Chef

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:39.100
who made the Golden Ratio shumai.

00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:40.190
What kind of unique buns

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:42.480
will he make?

00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:47.460
And, the progenitor of buns,

00:18:47.740 --> 00:18:49.230
the Pastry King from Bailuo family,

00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:50.490
what will his secret buns

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:51.540
be like?

00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:56.030
I’m so lucky to see

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:57.750
such a wonderful battle!

00:18:57.960 --> 00:18:59.370
You didn’t change at all.

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:01.440
No matter what the situation is,

00:19:01.580 --> 00:19:02.580
when you see superb skills

00:19:02.920 --> 00:19:04.060
or good dishes,

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:06.470
you sincerely praise them.

00:19:06.960 --> 00:19:09.240
That’s the greatest merit of you.

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:12.470
He is just a cooking nerd.

00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:37.340
Liu Maoxing.

00:19:38.160 --> 00:19:39.370
Tonight you will taste the pain

00:19:39.420 --> 00:19:41.280
of failure.

00:19:42.560 --> 00:19:43.820
The legendary cookware

00:19:43.930 --> 00:19:45.810
will belong to Dark Cooking Society,

00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:48.830
as well as Shanghai.

00:20:05.400 --> 00:20:07.230
Both sides have finished, right?

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:08.170
Of course.

00:20:08.550 --> 00:20:09.340
Yes.

00:20:13.720 --> 00:20:15.330
The number one dim sum chef in the Continent.

00:20:15.960 --> 00:20:17.750
And the last of the legendary Bailuo family.

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:21.100
This ultimate battle between dim sum chefs

00:20:21.150 --> 00:20:23.120
will have a great impact

00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:25.020
on the cooking world.

00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:34.370
This is a good opportunity.

00:20:34.780 --> 00:20:36.700
Before the top dim sum, you will know

00:20:36.890 --> 00:20:38.460
how insignificant you are.

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:40.130
You’ll have the feeling of inferiority.

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:42.980
That’s exactly my word to you.

00:20:43.740 --> 00:20:45.430
I don't care, Pastry King.

00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:46.870
I will defeat you

00:20:46.920 --> 00:20:48.720
and be the number one on the Continent.

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:58.990
Time to taste and judge.

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:00.930
Please serve the dishes.

00:21:50.890 --> 00:21:52.110
That is...

00:23:14.934 --> 00:23:16.894
Preview of the next episode

00:23:17.912 --> 00:23:20.602
Whoa! What is this Chinese steamed bun?

00:23:21.089 --> 00:23:23.370
To my surprise, the Chinese steamed bun
that Xie Lu had made

00:23:23.454 --> 00:23:25.546
suddenly started laughing out loud.

00:23:26.152 --> 00:23:27.535
Next episode, Chūka Ichiban!

00:23:28.098 --> 00:23:30.406
Super Dim Sum Battle!

00:23:30.406 --> 00:23:31.697
The Ultimate Decision!

00:23:32.156 --> 00:23:33.500
It will definitely be interesting!
